# Every change needs owner review. The paths below are called out explicitly
# because they are the ones where a malicious or careless PR does real damage.
#
# Ordering matters: the LAST matching pattern wins.

* @mikezupper

# CI runs on pull_request, so a PR can change what CI executes. The token is
# read-only and the repo holds no secrets, but a workflow edit still deserves
# a deliberate look.
/.github/ @mikezupper

# These run on a maintainer's machine, with their credentials, against their
# filesystem.
/scripts/ @mikezupper

# Points at the upstream beads repository. Redirecting this URL would make
# `update-beads.sh` fetch from somewhere else entirely.
/.gitmodules @mikezupper

# The highest-value target in this repo: agents EXECUTE what these files say.
# A destructive `bd` invocation added here -- a stray `--force`, a `bd init
# --reinit-local`, a `bd flatten` -- would be run against real issue databases
# by anything that loads the skill. Review command examples as if they were
# code, because they are.
/skills/ @mikezupper
